**Theorem 4.5**.: _Assume that \(\Omega\) is a bounded polygon and suppose \(\mathcal{T}_{h}\) is a uniformly regular triangulation of \(\bar{\Omega}\). If the solution \((\mathbf{u},p)\) of the Stokes Problem (2.1) has the regularity:_

\[\mathbf{u}\!\in\!H^{k+1}(\Omega)^{2},\ \ \ \ \ p\!\in\!H^{k}(\Omega)\cap L_{0}^{2}( \Omega)\ \ \ \ \mbox{for some $k\!\in\![1,l]$},\]

_then the solution \(p_{h}\) of Problem (4.72) satisfies the error estimate:_

(4.73) \[\|\,p\,-\,p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\leq Ch^{k}\{|\mathbf{u}|_{k+1,\Omega}+\,|p|_{k, \Omega}\}.\]

Proof.: In view of (4.10), for each \(q_{h}\) in \(Q_{h}\) we have:

\[\begin{split}\left|\int_{\Omega}(q_{h}-p_{h})\,\mathrm{div}\, \mathbf{v}_{h}\,dx\right|\leq&\ \|\,q_{h}-p\,\|_{0,\Omega}\|\,\mathrm{div}\,\mathbf{v}_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\\ &+\,v\|\,\sigma-\sigma_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\!\left(\sum\limits_{ \mathbf{v}\in\mathcal{T}_{h}}|\mathbf{v}_{h}|_{1,\kappa}^{2}\right)^{1/2}\\ &+\,v\|\,M_{n}(\sigma-\sigma_{h})\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}\|S(\mathbf{ v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}.\end{split}\]

Then, according to the inf-sup condition, we can choose \(\mathbf{v}_{h}\) in \(D_{0h}\) such that

\[\begin{split}\|\,q_{h}-p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}^{2}\leq& \ C_{1}\{\|\,q_{h}-p\|_{0,\Omega}+\,v\|\,\sigma-\sigma_{h}\|_{0, \Omega}\}\,\|\,q_{h}-p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\\ &+\,v\,\|\,M_{n}(\sigma-\sigma_{h})\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}\|\,S( \mathbf{v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}.\end{split}\]

It remains to estimate \(S(\mathbf{v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})\). To this end, we use the fact that

\[\mathbf{v}_{h}=\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}\]

with \(\mathrm{div}\,\mathbf{v}=q_{h}-p_{h}\), \(|\mathbf{v}|_{1,\Omega}\leq C_{2}\,\|\,q_{h}-p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\), \(\mathbf{v}\!\in\!H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)^{2}\).

Since \(S(\mathbf{v}\cdot\mathbf{t})=0\) we can write

\[S(\mathbf{v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})=S((\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}-\mathbf{v})\cdot \mathbf{t}).\]

Hence the argument of Theorem 4.4 gives:

\[\|\,S(\mathbf{v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})\|_{0,\kappa}\leq C_{3}(\rho_{\kappa})^{- 1/2}\{\|\,\partial\partial\hat{v}_{1}/\partial\hat{x}_{2}\,\|_{0,\hat{\kappa} }^{2}+\,\|\,\partial\hat{v}_{2}/\partial\hat{x}_{1}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}+\, \|\,\mathrm{div}\,\mathbf{\hat{v}}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}\}^{1/2}.\]

Therefore

\[\|\,S(\mathbf{v}_{h}\cdot\mathbf{t})\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}\leq C_{4}h^{1/2}\|\,q_ {h}-p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\]

and consequently,

\[\|\,q_{h}-p_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\leq C_{5}\{\|\,q_{h}-p\|_{0,\Omega}+\,v\|\,\sigma- \sigma_{h}\|_{0,\,h}\}.\]

Then (4.73) follows from (4.43) and Lemma A.5 or (A.51).

Observe that just (4.43) requires the uniformity of \(\mathcal{T}_{h}\). 

_Remark 4.6_.: It is also possible to associate this discontinuous approximation of the pressure with the "stream function-vorticity" scheme studied in SS2. The discrete version of the first equation (2.13) is:

\[Find\ p_{h}\!\in\!Q_{h},\mbox{defined by \eqref{eq:v_h}, solution of}\] (4.74) \[(p_{h},\mathrm{div}\,\mathbf{v}_{h})=v(\mathbf{curl}\,\mathbf{c}_{h}, \mathbf{v}_{h})-(\mathbf{f},\mathbf{v}_{h})\ \ \ \ \ \forall\mathbf{v}_{h}\!\in\!D_{0h}.\]
